{"id":"e04t3","name":"Monthly Cohort Retention","lang":"sql","entry":null,"params":[],"limit_s":10,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The growth team measures how many new customers order again the month after their first order. You have the table <b>orders</b> with the columns <code>order_id</code>, <code>customer_id</code>, <code>ordered_at</code> (timestamp) and <code>status</code> (<code>'delivered'</code> or <code>'cancelled'</code>). Cancelled orders never count.</p>\n<p>The <b>cohort</b> of a customer is the month of their first counted order. A customer is <b>retained</b> if they have at least one counted order in the calendar month just after their cohort month.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return, for every cohort, the columns <code>cohort_month</code> (text, <code>'YYYY-MM'</code>), <code>customers</code> (number of customers in the cohort), <code>retained</code> and <code>retention_pct</code> (<code>100 * retained / customers</code>, rounded to 1 decimal), sorted by <code>cohort_month</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>Table <code>orders</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>order_id</th><th>customer_id</th><th>ordered_at</th><th>status</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>2026-01-05 10:00:00</td><td>delivered</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>2026-02-01 09:00:00</td><td>delivered</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>2</td><td>2026-01-20 10:00:00</td><td>delivered</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>2</td><td>2026-03-02 10:00:00</td><td>delivered</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>3</td><td>2026-01-31 23:59:00</td><td>delivered</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>3</td><td>2026-02-28 12:00:00</td><td>cancelled</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>4</td><td>2026-02-10 10:00:00</td><td>delivered</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>4</td><td>2026-03-31 10:00:00</td><td>delivered</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>5</td><td>2026-01-02 10:00:00</td><td>cancelled</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>5</td><td>2026-02-03 10:00:00</td><td>delivered</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>cohort_month</th><th>customers</th><th>retained</th><th>retention_pct</th></tr><tr><td>2026-01</td><td>3</td><td>1</td><td>33.3</td></tr><tr><td>2026-02</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>50.0</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 10 seconds (psql)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB</div>","starter":"/* Write your PostgreSQL query here */\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["cohorte","date_trunc","LEFT JOIN","division entière","statut annulé"],"minutes":15,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"tables":{"orders":{"columns":[["order_id","INT"],["customer_id","INT"],["ordered_at","TIMESTAMP"],["status","VARCHAR(10)"]],"rows":[[1,1,"2026-01-05 10:00:00","delivered"],[2,1,"2026-02-01 09:00:00","delivered"],[3,2,"2026-01-20 10:00:00","delivered"],[4,2,"2026-03-02 10:00:00","delivered"],[5,3,"2026-01-31 23:59:00","delivered"],[6,3,"2026-02-28 12:00:00","cancelled"],[7,4,"2026-02-10 10:00:00","delivered"],[8,4,"2026-03-31 10:00:00","delivered"],[9,5,"2026-01-02 10:00:00","cancelled"],[10,5,"2026-02-03 10:00:00","delivered"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["cohort_month","customers","retained","retention_pct"],"rows":[["2026-01",3,1,33.3],["2026-02",2,1,50.0]]}},{"input":{"tables":{"orders":{"columns":[["order_id","INT"],["customer_id","INT"],["ordered_at","TIMESTAMP"],["status","VARCHAR(10)"]],"rows":[[1,9,"2025-12-31 23:00:00","delivered"],[2,9,"2026-01-01 01:00:00","delivered"],[3,8,"2025-12-15 10:00:00","delivered"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["cohort_month","customers","retained","retention_pct"],"rows":[["2025-12",2,1,50.0]]}}],"hidden_n":7,"hidden":"","solution":""}